 "story": {
  "title": "A corn belt waltz",
  "lede": "Central Iowa is corn and soybeans almost wall to wall. NISAR watched a full year.",
  "body": [
   "From bare fields in May to the peak of the canopy in late September, HV climbed about 8 dB as leaves and stalks filled the fields with scatterers. One pass after harvest began, it had fallen 4 dB.",
   "In January, frozen ground darkened the fields: ice holds less liquid water, so the soil sends less of the radar back.",
   "Medians over about 81,000 cultivated hectares north of Ames."
